sentences.text:
The petitioner is directed to be enlarged on bail in Crime No.60/2023 of Bidar Women Police Station, Bidar, registered for the offences punishable under Sections 363, 376, 366 and 376(2)(n) of IPC and under Sections 4,
6, 8 and 12 of the POCSO Act, pending in Special case (POCSO) No.7/2024 on the file of learned Additional District and Sessions judge at Bidar, subject to the following conditions:
a) The petitioner shall execute personal bond for a sum of Rs.1,00,000/- with two sureties for the likesum, to the satisfaction of the jurisdictional Court;
b) The petitioner shall appear regularly on all the dates of hearing before the Trial Court unless the Trial Court exempts his appearance for valid reasons;
Bablukumar vs The State Of Karnataka And Anr on 14 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/94455478/
3 c) The petitioner shall not directly or indirectly threaten or tamper with the prosecution witnesses;
d) The petitioner shall not involve in similar offences in future;
NC: 2024:KHC-K:3874 e) The petitioner shall not leave the jurisdiction of the Trial Court without permission of the said Court until the case registered against him is disposed off.
Sd/-
JUDGE SRT Bablukumar vs The State Of Karnataka And Anr on 14 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/94455478/
